A||||7||mrfixit58||Bored Out Intake and Throttle Body||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||09-12-2001||04:36 PM||||Is there any advantage to installing a bored out throttle body and intake to a stock 2.8? If you combine it with bored out exhaust manifolds wouldn't you see a little more top end Hp? If you increased the fuel pressure would it help? Has anyone done this and if so, what does your Seat-O-Pants meter tell you? <BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||09-12-2001||08:03 PM||||Before i got my 3.2 i had the bored out t-body and upper plenum on my original 2.8<BR>and there was a very noticable difference<BR>in performance! I think it makes a bigger difference on a bigger engine but it's definitely worth while on te 2.8 as well.<P>I can't comment on the ported manifold from experience because I waited for the new engine to put on a set of headers.<BR>I have heard that the ported manifolds do make a difference though which makes sense<BR>if you've ever looked at the inside of a stock set. The stock set is very restricted.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000002||88formula||09-12-2001||09:50 PM||||What most people notice is not the 2-3 horsepower increase in power that they get but the increase in throttle sensitivity that a bigger TB creates.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||09-13-2001||08:20 AM||||Thanks guys. I'm not trying to fool myself into thinking that by changing the TB and intake I can take on C5s. I'm just wondering if it's worthwile investment. It seems like it would be a fairly simple mod.<P>Dave - Did you have your manifolds hogged out at the same time, before of after?<P>Again, Thanks for your input.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Voytek||09-13-2001||03:18 PM||||I don't think it's worth the while unless you're running full throttle (like at the track).<P>Think about it.  The only time you will actually be able to get in the extra air flow that the stock TB can't deliver, is when the throttle is near or fully open.  <P>The difference is that to get the same air flow with a std. TB you'll need to depress the gas pedal slightly more than with one that's bored out, i.e. you will still be getting the SAME volume of air flow only with a different pedal travel.  Does that make sense?<P>I would only invest in it if I was planning on doing some racing.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||09-13-2001||04:35 PM||||I have both a bored out TB and Intake Plenum (from Darrell Morse) as well as a ported stock exhaust manifold.  And YES, there is an increase in throttle response.  Darrell's TB flows about 13% more air.  With the bored out intake, it also has a larger volume of air "on tap" when you hit the pedal.  Go for it- it's worth it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||09-13-2001||08:58 PM||||I didn't get the manifolds ported I went with headers instead.<P>For those of you that don't think it works:<BR>you should give it a try and see what you're missing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||09-13-2001||08:59 PM||||I didn't get the manifolds ported I went with headers instead.<P>For those of you that don't think it works:<BR>you should give it a try and see what you're missing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
